# Ensures the public/ directory is tracked by git.
#
# Git does not track empty directories, and apps/web/public currently has no
# static assets. Without this file a fresh checkout (e.g. GitHub Actions)
# has no apps/web/public at all, which breaks the runner-stage COPY in
# apps/web/Dockerfile ("/repo/apps/web/public": not found). Next.js also
# expects the directory to exist.
#
# Real static assets can be added alongside this file at any time.
